Package: lindos-meta
Version: 1.0.0
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Lindos Team <team@lindos.dev>
Depends: lindos-core (= 1.0.0), lindos-desktop (= 1.0.0), lindos-setup (= 1.0.0), lindos-settings (= 1.0.0), lindos-compat (= 1.0.0), lindos-gaming (= 1.0.0), lindos-tune (= 1.0.0), lindos-transfer (= 1.0.0)
Recommends: lindos-kernel, lindos-vm, lindos-winapps, firefox, steam-launcher | steam-installer, wine-staging | wine, winetricks, gamemode, mangohud, gamescope, flatpak, xfce4-panel-profiles, xfce4-docklike-plugin, picom, earlyoom, power-profiles-daemon
Suggests: lutris, heroic, umu-launcher, corectrl, openrgb, nbfc-linux, scx
Homepage: https://lindos.dev
Description: Lindos 1.0 (Aurora) — complete Windows-11-style desktop remaster of Linux Mint XFCE
 Meta package that pulls in every Lindos component: the core library and
 helper (lindos-core), the theme/panel/branding (lindos-desktop), the
 first-boot OOBE wizard (lindos-setup), the Settings centre (lindos-settings),
 Windows-app support through Wine/Proton (lindos-compat), gaming launchers and
 drivers (lindos-gaming), the RAM/performance tuning (lindos-tune) and a
 Windows Easy Transfer-style migration tool (lindos-transfer).
 .
 lindos-compat also opens every other common Windows file type (MSIX/APPX
 packages and bundles, .msp patches, .reg, .ps1, .vbs, .url, .scr, .cpl, .inf,
 .cab, disk images, DOS and 16-bit programs, "./setup.exe" from a terminal)
 and can install packages by id with 'lindos-compat winget install' — hash-
 verified straight from each publisher's own manifest, HTTPS only, no
 override. For games whose kernel-level anti-cheat cannot run on any Linux
 (Valorant, League of Legends, Call of Duty, and the like), lindos-game route
 shows the honest way to actually play them: an official cloud-streaming
 service where one exists, or a one-command restart into the PC's own
 Windows installation (lindos-dualboot, a genuine UEFI/GRUB one-shot boot,
 never a VM trick and never a Windows edit) — never an emulator or spoofer,
 because none can produce the hardware-rooted signature those anti-cheats
 verify.
 .
 The Lindos-tuned kernel (lindos-kernel: ntsync, sched_ext, 1000 Hz preempt,
 MGLRU) is Recommended, not required — the stock Mint/Ubuntu kernel stays
 installed as a fallback and the Lindos kernel is selected in grub only when
 its compiled image is actually present.
 .
 For software that genuinely needs Windows, two more components are Recommended
 (both optional, both requiring a user-supplied licensed Windows): lindos-vm, an
 honest KVM/QEMU Windows virtual machine with optional GPU passthrough, and
 lindos-winapps, which shows individual Windows programs (Adobe, Office) as
 seamless windows over RDP. Neither ships or performs any VM-detection evasion,
 hardware/SMBIOS spoofing or licence bypass, and neither defeats VM-blocking
 anti-cheat (Vanguard and the like) — that is impossible and is not attempted.
 .
 Honesty notes: Windows programs run through Wine/Proton (a translation
 layer, not Windows and not a VM); Valorant and Fortnite do not run on any
 Linux; Roblox runs through Sober; Edge/Chrome are downloaded from the vendor
 while Lindos installs (Firefox ships on the ISO); the idle RAM target is 350-500 MB.
 No anti-cheat circumvention of any kind is shipped or possible.
